  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "An array is called lovely if the sum of product of each adjacent pair of elements is odd.\n\nMore formally, the array SSS of size MMM is lovely if the value ∑i=1M−1\\sum_{i=1}^{M-1}∑i=1M−1​ (Si.Si+1)(S_i . S_{i+1})(Si​.Si+1​) is **odd**.\n\nYou are given an array AAA consisting of NNN positive integers. Find a permutation of array AAA which is lovely.\n\nIf multiple such permutations are possible, output any. If there is no lovely permutation, output `-1`.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains an integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The TTT test cases then follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, if a lovely permutation of AAA is possible, print a single line containing NNN integers denoting the elements of any lovely permutation of AAA. Otherwise, print `-1`.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\le T \\le 10001≤T≤1000",
      "2≤N≤5002 \\le N \\le 5002≤N≤500",
      "1≤Ai≤1061 \\le A_i \\le 10^61≤Ai​≤106",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 1 (100 points):** Original constraints."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n5\n1 2 3 4 10\n3\n7 11 145",
        "output": "3 1 10 2 4\n-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: The sum of products of adjacent pair of elements of the given array is 1⋅2+2⋅3+3⋅4+4⋅10=2+6+12+40=601\\cdot 2 + 2\\cdot 3 + 3\\cdot 4 + 4\\cdot 10 = 2+6+12+40 = 601⋅2+2⋅3+3⋅4+4⋅10=2+6+12+40=60. Since this value is even, this is not a lovely permutation of the array.\nA lovely permutation of the given array is [3,1,10,2,4][3, 1, 10, 2, 4][3,1,10,2,4]. The sum of products for this array would be 3⋅1+1⋅10+10⋅2+2⋅4=413\\cdot 1 + 1\\cdot 10 + 10\\cdot 2 + 2\\cdot 4 = 413⋅1+1⋅10+10⋅2+2⋅4=41, which is odd.\nTest Case 222: No permutation of the given array exists where the sum of products of adjacent pair of elements is odd. Thus, answer is −1-1−1."
      }
    ]
  },
